1
00:00:03,333 --> 00:00:07,400
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:09,333 --> 00:00:14,933
So... The controls are busted,
the fence is electrified,

3
00:00:14,933 --> 00:00:19,567
I don't know where the power source
is, AND I'm still lock-blocked.

4
00:00:19,567 --> 00:00:24,800
What we have here is a multi-layered
problem, except there's no actual solution.

5
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:29,533
Or at least, none within the confines
of the p--Whoa! Don't touch that!

6
00:00:29,533 --> 00:00:35,200
It's happening again. I keep coming back
to this feeling that I'm a rat in a maze.

7
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:37,300
Except it's all dead ends.

8
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:40,033
You put rats in mazes
to teach them something.

9
00:00:40,033 --> 00:00:42,000
What am I supposed to be learning here?

10
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,067
That...life is bullshit!

11
00:00:44,533 --> 00:00:46,333
Apparently I needed to learn that!

12
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:47,833
A refresher!

13
00:00:49,067 --> 00:00:49,800
Fuck...

14
00:00:50,867 --> 00:00:51,767
Yeah! That's me!

15
00:00:51,767 --> 00:00:54,500
Just too pie-in-the-sky, Pollyanna-singing--

16
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:55,467
[explosions]
OH!

17
00:00:57,967 --> 00:00:58,398
What?

18
00:00:59,190 --> 00:01:00,000
[alarm ringing]

19
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,967
[alarm ringing]
Oh, there's an alarm? That's hilarious.

20
00:01:02,967 --> 00:01:04,700
Yeah, come get me, guys.

21
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:05,767
[low-pitched humming]

22
00:01:05,767 --> 00:01:06,850
Holy shit!

23
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:09,340
That didn't do much.

24
00:01:09,833 --> 00:01:11,733
Alright, you know what?
It doesn't even matter.

25
00:01:11,733 --> 00:01:15,300
They're headed that way, I'm going
downriver, it's all going to work out.

26
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:18,900
So there WAS a solution. I just
needed to blow up everything.

27
00:01:18,900 --> 00:01:21,767
The answer was right in
front of me this whole time.

28
00:01:21,767 --> 00:01:23,300
[gunfire]
Jesus! How...?

29
00:01:23,300 --> 00:01:25,467
Whatever. I'll tell you
what I told your friend:

30
00:01:25,467 --> 00:01:27,167
GRENAAAAAADE!

31
00:01:27,167 --> 00:01:27,800
METROCOP #1: That's a grenade!

32
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:28,400
Uh-huh.

33
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:30,367
GRENAAAAAA--! Oh, shit.

34
00:01:30,367 --> 00:01:31,967
Oh wait. That's just a cam bot.

35
00:01:31,967 --> 00:01:33,800
[explosion]
It's getting caught in the doorwa--.

36
00:01:34,567 --> 00:01:35,833
No.

37
00:01:35,833 --> 00:01:37,067
No!

38
00:01:37,067 --> 00:01:37,933
NO!

39
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:40,700
Okay, I've reloaded!
You can keep coming now!

40
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:42,333
Actually, I have a better idea.

41
00:01:42,333 --> 00:01:46,100
Oh, NOW you show up! We need to
coordinate! This isn't working!

42
00:01:47,567 --> 00:01:48,800
Yeah, that's a little better.

43
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:52,400
Next time, wait until my gun's
out, THEN come through the doorway.

44
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:57,033
Those first two guys were right on
cue. You're a three out of ten, man.

45
00:01:57,033 --> 00:01:58,400
Okay...

46
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:01,033
Oh, whoops! I didn't even think about that.

47
00:02:01,033 --> 00:02:01,833
[explosion]

48
00:02:01,833 --> 00:02:04,267
It's just becoming reflex at this point.

49
00:02:04,267 --> 00:02:06,933
Y'know, I kind of hope
that bot WAS recording

50
00:02:06,940 --> 00:02:09,433
because that had to look bad ass:

51
00:02:09,440 --> 00:02:13,100
gun right at the camera, me
looking stone-cold killer...

52
00:02:13,100 --> 00:02:15,133
If they're going to make
wanted posters of me,

53
00:02:15,133 --> 00:02:17,200
they HAVE to use that shot.

54
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:18,333
I mean, they HAVE to.

55
00:02:18,867 --> 00:02:20,400
OH! I WHIFFED IT!

56
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:21,800
That's okay, I have more.

57
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:23,600
[explosion, Combine chatter]

58
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:25,000
I hear them chattering.

59
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:27,433
I can't believe they got here so fast!

60
00:02:27,433 --> 00:02:29,567
They must've radioed as soon as they saw me;

61
00:02:29,567 --> 00:02:31,467
that alarm was just a coincidence.

62
00:02:31,467 --> 00:02:34,400
Even cop-killers can't
get service THAT fast.

63
00:02:34,400 --> 00:02:35,633
[Combine chatter]
OH!

64
00:02:35,633 --> 00:02:36,600
[Combine chatter]

65
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:38,180
Oh, just shut up!

66
00:02:38,767 --> 00:02:39,700
METROCOP #2: That's a grenade!

67
00:02:40,433 --> 00:02:41,354
TA-DA!

68
00:02:41,933 --> 00:02:44,300
Oh, that was a crap toss. My bad!

69
00:02:44,300 --> 00:02:45,600
[explosion]
WHOA!

70
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:47,667
Michelin's revenge.

71
00:02:47,667 --> 00:02:50,000
Oh, good. You're back. Let's try this again.

72
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:50,700
Pick it up!

73
00:02:50,700 --> 00:02:50,967
METROCOP #3: Grena--

74
00:02:50,967 --> 00:02:51,700
[explosion]

75
00:02:51,700 --> 00:02:54,933
Perfect. See? I'm getting better at this.

76
00:02:54,933 --> 00:02:56,367
METROCOP #4: That's a grenade!

77
00:02:56,367 --> 00:02:56,967
[explosion]

78
00:02:56,967 --> 00:03:00,033
But you know what my problem
is? I need more grenades.

79
00:03:00,033 --> 00:03:02,267
Yeah, I feel much more comfortable now.

80
00:03:02,267 --> 00:03:04,833
I like how I seem to be
steering the conversation.

81
00:03:04,833 --> 00:03:07,700
Before it was "hostiles"
or "What's your location?"

82
00:03:07,700 --> 00:03:09,267
Now it's all "Grenades!"

83
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:11,400
All grenades!

84
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:13,767
Welcome to Grenadier
Gordon's Grenade Emporium!

85
00:03:13,767 --> 00:03:16,300
Our prices are so low,
we're giving 'em away!

86
00:03:16,300 --> 00:03:17,433
[explosions]
HAVE A GRENADE!

87
00:03:17,433 --> 00:03:18,567
[explosions]
GIVE ONE TO YOU FRIENDS!

88
00:03:18,567 --> 00:03:19,267
[explosions]

89
00:03:19,267 --> 00:03:19,767
[explosions]
Shit...

90
00:03:19,767 --> 00:03:21,400
[explosions]
GIVE ONE TO YOUR FAMILY!

91
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:23,000
[explosions]
GIVE ONE TO YOUR NEIGHBOR!

92
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:25,172
[explosions]
GIVE ONE TO YOUR BOSS!

93
00:03:25,172 --> 00:03:26,700
[explosions]
Ah! Fuck you...!

94
00:03:28,467 --> 00:03:30,100
[explosion]
Blah!

95
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:33,733
Well, for our less-discerning
customers, we also have bullets.

96
00:03:33,733 --> 00:03:36,567
Grenades require a more refined palate.

97
00:03:36,567 --> 00:03:37,139
Ah!

98
00:03:38,649 --> 00:03:41,367
Don't try to haggle with me, you savages!

99
00:03:41,367 --> 00:03:42,900
ALL PRICES ARE FINAL!

100
00:03:42,900 --> 00:03:45,633
I only purchase from reputable suppliers,

101
00:03:45,633 --> 00:03:48,967
like...dead people giving
me loads of free stuff.

102
00:03:48,967 --> 00:03:50,933
This is much better business.

103
00:03:50,933 --> 00:03:53,200
Although if I'm being honest with myself,

104
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:58,573
if I had to criticize these grenades,
it's that they blink red and make noises.

105
00:03:58,573 --> 00:04:01,200
Somebody was trying to express themselves

106
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:05,033
when it's a classic case of the
designer not actually being a user.

107
00:04:05,033 --> 00:04:08,533
But I'll still take more!
I didn't even notice that.

108
00:04:08,533 --> 00:04:10,967
Hell, this saves me a trip
back to the other room.

109
00:04:10,967 --> 00:04:14,500
I mean, I was never leaving here
without several of my closest friends.

110
00:04:14,500 --> 00:04:17,500
But yeah, I saw this all
the time at Black Mesa.

111
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:20,267
Like that microwave gun people
would keep walking in front of

112
00:04:20,267 --> 00:04:22,000
because nobody knew it was on,

113
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:26,400
or those guided missiles that would fly out
of range from the authentication servers...

114
00:04:26,400 --> 00:04:29,167
The Pentagon was PISSED about that one!

115
00:04:29,167 --> 00:04:31,233
Oh, and of course the laser tank...

116
00:04:31,233 --> 00:04:32,505
Okay, focus...

117
00:04:33,600 --> 00:04:34,767
Hup! Hup!

118
00:04:34,767 --> 00:04:38,167
Yeah, it would refract and melt the
gunner when the lens got cracked

119
00:04:38,167 --> 00:04:39,600
so that was another no-go.

120
00:04:39,600 --> 00:04:42,967
They should've made the grenades look
like rocks or potatoes or something,

121
00:04:42,967 --> 00:04:44,100
then the cops would be like,

122
00:04:44,100 --> 00:04:47,033
[mocking voice]
"Oh look. He's throwing potatoes at us. Hoho..."

123
00:04:47,033 --> 00:04:48,700
Hot potato, bitch.

124
00:04:48,700 --> 00:04:51,333
I still can't get over
how fast they got here.

125
00:04:51,333 --> 00:04:55,233
These cops make so many mistakes, maybe
that's the one thing they do right.

126
00:04:55,233 --> 00:04:57,767
Like how Domino's
promises 30 minutes or less,

127
00:04:57,767 --> 00:04:59,967
maybe here, from the time you dial 9-1-1,

128
00:04:59,967 --> 00:05:03,833
they pride themselves on arriving to put
a bullet in your head in under 15 minutes.

129
00:05:03,840 --> 00:05:05,620
God, I fucking hate cops.

130
00:05:07,560 --> 00:05:10,600
No, wait. It wouldn't be 9-1-1. I'm in Europe.

131
00:05:10,600 --> 00:05:12,300
I don't know what number they are.

132
00:05:12,300 --> 00:05:15,667
Okay, I'm just going to time this right,

133
00:05:15,667 --> 00:05:19,567
otherwise this could be the
most casual beheading ever.

134
00:05:19,567 --> 00:05:22,267
My suit would brace my head like a golf tee.

135
00:05:22,267 --> 00:05:24,100
Actually, I'm being a pessimist.

136
00:05:24,100 --> 00:05:26,700
The boat seems strong enough
to absorb some of the force,

137
00:05:26,700 --> 00:05:29,633
so the beam would probably
just crush my skull instead.

138
00:05:29,633 --> 00:05:30,767
[distant gunfire]
Oh, this again.

139
00:05:30,767 --> 00:05:32,400
Well, I have glasses.

140
00:05:32,400 --> 00:05:34,700
AH! AH! HE'S HITTING THE FRAME!

141
00:05:34,700 --> 00:05:35,600
Oof!

142
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:38,433
SHIIIIIYYAAAAAAAAH!

143
00:05:38,433 --> 00:05:39,333
OOF!

144
00:05:39,333 --> 00:05:41,067
OH MY GOD! ROCKETS!

145
00:05:41,067 --> 00:05:42,667
I THOUGHT WE WERE PAST THAT!

146
00:05:42,667 --> 00:05:45,000
YOU'RE SHOWING NO PERSONAL GROWTH AT ALL!

147
00:05:45,800 --> 00:05:48,067
AND DON'T GET ME STARTED ON YOU!

148
00:05:48,067 --> 00:05:50,900
I'm not even going to look back
to see if a rocket's following me!

149
00:05:51,633 --> 00:05:52,067
What?!

150
00:05:53,300 --> 00:05:54,467
What's happening?!

151
00:05:54,467 --> 00:05:55,800
Why would they do that?!

152
00:05:55,800 --> 00:05:57,200
They think they're Spider-Man?!

153
00:05:57,800 --> 00:05:58,467
STOP IT!

154
00:05:59,233 --> 00:06:00,300
They're right in the wa--

155
00:06:00,933 --> 00:06:02,767
YOU'RE NOT SPIDER-MAN!

156
00:06:02,767 --> 00:06:06,867
No, no! C'mon, YOU KNOW I
HATE ROCKETS! YOU KNOW THIS!

157
00:06:07,633 --> 00:06:07,967
HOOH!

158
00:06:08,367 --> 00:06:10,233
THAT WAS A BEARD-TRIMMER!

159
00:06:10,233 --> 00:06:12,300
Oh, my God! I'm in a kill-zone!

160
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:14,409
IT'S TOO LATE! WE ALL BURN!

161
00:06:15,067 --> 00:06:15,833
Uff!

162
00:06:15,833 --> 00:06:18,100
OH MY GOD! I'M AMAZING!

163
00:06:18,100 --> 00:06:19,600
WHOA-WHOA-WHOA!

164
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:21,467
WHO THREW A CAR AT ME?!

165
00:06:21,467 --> 00:06:23,800
DID GOD JUST THROW A CAR AT ME?!

166
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:24,533
WHY?!

167
00:06:24,533 --> 00:06:26,667
Well, there's probably a lot of reasons...

168
00:06:26,667 --> 00:06:27,167
Dah!

169
00:06:27,167 --> 00:06:29,600
But that's what Looney Tunes God would do!

170
00:06:29,600 --> 00:06:30,567
DAAAAH!

171
00:06:30,567 --> 00:06:32,733
GET AWAY! GET AWAY!

172
00:06:32,733 --> 00:06:33,911
Are they coming for me?!

173
00:06:34,800 --> 00:06:40,333
Hey...this is actually...pretty
for a...filthy drainage canal.

174
00:06:40,333 --> 00:06:42,033
Oh, that was everything...

175
00:06:42,040 --> 00:06:43,740
There's too much everything.

176
00:06:43,740 --> 00:06:46,433
I mean, what DIDN'T they throw at me?

177
00:06:46,433 --> 00:06:49,133
Okay, they didn't send guys on jet skis.

178
00:06:49,133 --> 00:06:52,633
But that's just because
the--OOF!--because the water's low.

179
00:06:52,633 --> 00:06:54,721
I'm sure they have them in storage.

180
00:06:55,633 --> 00:06:57,633
Okay, c'mon! I don't have
time for this shit!

181
00:06:57,633 --> 00:07:00,700
THEY ARE ON MY ASS! I'VE GOTTA KEEP MOVING!

182
00:07:00,700 --> 00:07:04,000
In fact, that changes
everything. I NEED the boat.

183
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:06,867
They have assault vehicles
with homing rockets!

184
00:07:06,867 --> 00:07:11,933
I'd be lucky to survive that in a tank,
forget on foot in all these open plains.

185
00:07:11,933 --> 00:07:15,033
Those are my choices. Would you
like some death with your death?

186
00:07:15,033 --> 00:07:16,200
WUAH! Oof!

187
00:07:16,200 --> 00:07:17,067
No, thank you!

188
00:07:17,067 --> 00:07:18,867
Hold the death, please!

189
00:07:18,867 --> 00:07:23,033
Oh, no no no no no no NO NO NO NOOOOOO!

190
00:07:23,033 --> 00:07:24,533
ARE YOU ACTUALLY...?!

191
00:07:25,633 --> 00:07:26,500
FUUUCK!

192
00:07:26,500 --> 00:07:28,167
[alarms blaring]

193
00:07:28,167 --> 00:07:31,366
[alarms blaring]
Well...back to work.

194
00:07:31,366 --> 00:07:34,133
[alarms blaring]

195
00:07:34,133 --> 00:07:34,750
[alarms blaring]
Hey...

196
00:07:34,750 --> 00:07:36,067
[alarms blaring]

197
00:07:36,067 --> 00:07:37,383
[alarms blaring]
I think those are the same alarms

198
00:07:37,383 --> 00:07:38,825
[alarms blaring]
we had at Black Mesa.

199
00:07:38,825 --> 00:07:40,067
[alarms blaring]

200
00:07:40,067 --> 00:07:40,700
[alarms blaring]
Huh.

201
00:07:40,700 --> 00:07:42,567
[alarms blaring]

